{"id":"b4","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":4,"of":9,"title":"The word with no meaning","titleHe":"אֶת","goal":"Use אֶת before a definite direct object.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"אֶת has no translation. It marks the direct object of a verb — but only when that object is definite. It's one of the commonest words in Hebrew and one of the last a learner uses correctly."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אֲנִי רוֹאֶה בַּיִת.","en":"I see a house. — no אֶת"},{"he":"אֲנִי רוֹאֶה אֶת הַבַּיִת.","en":"I see the house. — definite, so אֶת"},{"he":"הִיא אוֹהֶבֶת אֶת דָּוִד.","en":"She loves David. — names are definite"}]},{"type":"text","body":"With a pronoun it declines, and those forms are how you say me, him, them as objects."},{"type":"table","caption":"אֶת with endings","head":["","form"],"rows":[["me","אוֹתִי"],["you (m.)","אוֹתְךָ"],["you (f.)","אוֹתָךְ"],["him / it","אוֹתוֹ"],["her","אוֹתָהּ"],["us","אוֹתָנוּ"],["them","אוֹתָם"]]}],"vocab":[{"he":"אֶת","en":"(marks a definite object)","translit":"et"},{"he":"אוֹתִי","en":"me","translit":"oti"},{"he":"אוֹתוֹ","en":"him, it","translit":"oto"},{"he":"אוֹתָהּ","en":"her","translit":"ota"},{"he":"רוֹאֶה","en":"sees","translit":"ro'e"},{"he":"שׁוֹמֵעַ","en":"hears","translit":"shome'a"},{"he":"יוֹדֵעַ","en":"knows","translit":"yode'a"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["son","please, you're welcome","is located, is found","(marks a definite object)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אֶת","translit":"et"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["me","deed, work","everything","school"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אוֹתִי","translit":"oti"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["him, it","then","to, for","man"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אוֹתוֹ","translit":"oto"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["a little","her","books","next to"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אוֹתָהּ","translit":"ota"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["loves, likes","sees","gets up","dog"],"correct":1,"prompt":"רוֹאֶה","translit":"ro'e"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["hears","houses","beautiful","teacher (f.)"],"correct":0,"prompt":"שׁוֹמֵעַ","translit":"shome'a"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["book","number","knows","synagogue"],"correct":2,"prompt":"יוֹדֵעַ","translit":"yode'a"},{"type":"choice","q":"them?","options":["אוֹתִי","אוֹתָם","אוֹתָךְ","אוֹתְךָ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"him / it?","options":["אוֹתִי","אוֹתָךְ","אוֹתְךָ","אוֹתוֹ"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “her”?","options":["אוֹתָהּ","אֵינֶנִּי","שֶׁמֶשׁ","בֵּן"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"her?","options":["אוֹתִי","אוֹתְךָ","אוֹתָךְ","אוֹתָהּ"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “him, it”?","options":["סִפּוּר","יָכוֹל","הוּא","אוֹתוֹ"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “me”?","options":["אוֹתִי","גַּם","אָח","מְדֻבָּר"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["יוֹדֵעַ","אוֹתוֹ","אוֹתָהּ","אֶת"],"correct":3,"say":"אֶת","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “(marks a definite object)”?","options":["מְקַבֵּל","מְסֻדָּר","אֶת","טֶרֶם"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"אוֹתָהּ","translit":"ota","en":"her"}]}